<h2 id='what-is-profitbooks'>🔍 What Is ProfitBooks?</h2>

ProfitBooks is a cloud-based accounting and inventory management platform built specifically for product-led small businesses. Unlike horizontal platforms like QuickBooks or Xero that bolt inventory on as an afterthought, ProfitBooks treats stock management as a first-class citizen — which matters enormously when you're running a jewelry or watch boutique where a single SKU can carry a $12,000 cost basis.

Founded in 2012, the platform has carved out a niche serving manufacturers, distributors, and retailers in high-SKU, high-value categories. The jewelry and luxury watch segment maps well onto its core architecture: serialized inventory tracking, multi-currency support for international wholesale purchasing, and margin-by-item reporting that most generalist accounting tools fumble.

The platform is browser-based with no desktop install required, and it connects to a modest but growing ecosystem of payment gateways, e-commerce platforms, and shipping tools. For boutiques running lean operations without a dedicated CFO or accounting staff, ProfitBooks positions itself as the system that handles the books *and* tells you which pieces are killing your margin.

