<h2 id='our-experience'>🧪 Our Experience Testing ProfitBooks</h2>

Our team has evaluated accounting and ERP software across dozens of luxury retail contexts — from single-door watch boutiques in secondary markets to multi-location fine jewelry chains with eight-figure revenues. We ran ProfitBooks through a structured evaluation that mirrors the actual workflows our operator community deals with daily: receiving consignment stock from brand partners, reconciling sales against serialized inventory, generating reports for quarterly tax prep, and issuing multi-currency purchase orders to European and Asian vendors.

We set up a representative test environment with 200 SKUs across three product categories (fine jewelry, watches, and accessories), loaded historical transaction data, and ran the platform through a full simulated month-end close. We also consulted with three independent boutique owners who have been running ProfitBooks as their primary accounting system for at least 12 months.

The headline finding: ProfitBooks performs above its price class on inventory-linked financial reporting, and below expectations on bank reconciliation UX. Both of those things matter to a jeweler trying to close the books without a full-time bookkeeper.

