<h2 id='who-its-for'>🎯 Who ProfitBooks Is (and Isn't) For</h2>

**ProfitBooks is the right call if:**

You're an independent jeweler or watch boutique operator doing $300K–$5M in annual revenue who needs real inventory-linked accounting without enterprise pricing. You buy from multiple vendors, carry serialized high-value stock, manage some consignment relationships, and you're currently either using spreadsheets, a badly configured QuickBooks file, or paying your accountant to clean up a mess every quarter.

You'll get the most out of ProfitBooks if you're willing to invest 4–8 hours in initial setup — configuring your product categories, tax codes, vendor records, and opening balances correctly. The platform rewards clean data.

**ProfitBooks is not the right fit if:**

You operate multiple locations and need location-level P&L reporting with consolidated views. ProfitBooks' multi-location support is limited, and our team would point multi-door operators toward more capable platforms. See our comparison of <a href='https://luxeretailstack.com/comparisons/accounting-software-multi-location-jewelry'>accounting software for multi-location jewelry retailers</a> for those use cases.

You need built-in payroll for U.S. employees, a native POS that syncs to accounting in real time, or deep e-commerce platform integrations beyond basic payment gateways. Those gaps exist and won't be papered over by ProfitBooks' other strengths.

