<h2 id='final-verdict'>🏁 Final Verdict</h2>

ProfitBooks earns its place in our recommended stack for independent jewelry and watch boutiques. The combination of serialized inventory, consignment tracking, multi-currency support, and item-level margin reporting — all at under $30/mo — is genuinely difficult to match at this price point. The gaps around bank reconciliation UX, POS integration, and multi-location reporting are real, but they're the right gaps for this platform's target customer to have workarounds for.

Our team's honest assessment: if you're a single-location boutique currently running your books in QuickBooks Online and paying $90/mo for features you use 20% of, switching to ProfitBooks will save you money and likely give you better inventory-financial integration in the process. If you're using spreadsheets or doing informal bookkeeping, ProfitBooks is the upgrade that will actually get done — it's not intimidating to non-accountants.

The 30-day free trial requires no credit card. We recommend spending that trial period importing one month of real transaction data rather than playing with demo data. That's when you'll see whether the platform fits your operation, and it puts you in a position to make a genuinely informed decision.

